Installation Instructions
=========================

Prerquisites
------------

1. Core Library

	- gcc
        - GNU make
        - debhelper (when building a Debian package)
        - fakeroot
        - pod2man


2. Perl Bindings

	- Perl (development package)


3. Python Bindings

	- cpio
	- Python (development package)
        - pip
        - setuptools


Procedure
---------

make
make install

All files will be installed below the top-level directory specifed in
the PREFIX file. Default is /usr/local, edit the file to change this.

The Makefile also supports the DESTDIR mechanism for relocating the
tree that's be installed at installation time.

make deb

can be used to build a Debian package.


Selecting Language Bindings
---------------------------

The BINDINGS variable in the file bindings/Makefile defines the
language bindings to build by default.


Test Suite
----------

Running

make test

in the top-level directory will run the test suite. The perl-based
tests have been written to test all features of the core library as
well, the Python ones only to test the Python language bindings.


Building Via Docker
-------------------

While this is probably a bit of a gimmick, the package can also be
built in a Docker container. Provided there's a working docker
installation on the build host, the script scripts/docker-build
can be used for this. It'll create a docker image

<username>/uni-json-base

This will be a Debian 12 (see docker/uni-json-base.dockerfile for
information how to change this) image containing all the software
necessary for building the package. A second image

<username>/uni-json

will be used to create a container for building the package based
on the current source, ie, without having to recreate the base
image for every build. After building completed, the tmp directory
will contain ready-to-install Debian packages and a tar.gz file
containing all the files with the PREFIX part of the path
removed.
